    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes \u2014 **59 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the business-day rule in `BusinessDay.java` to skip public holidays in addition to weekends.\n\n**Change:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BusinessDay.java`\n\n- Added a fixed `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` set: `2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28`.\n- Rewrote `adjust(...)` from the previous \"weekend \u2192 Monday\" jump into a loop that advances one day at a time while the date is a Saturday, Sunday, or listed holiday, until it reaches a non-holiday weekday.\n\nThe loop is what makes runs of adjacent non-business days work correctly \u2014 e.g. `2026-12-25` (Fri, holiday) \u2192 Sat/Sun \u2192 `2026-12-28` (Mon, holiday) \u2192 rolls all the way to `2026-12-29` (Tue). `effective(...)` is unchanged; it still calls `adjust`, so both a supplied date and the defaulted server date get the holiday roll-forward, and everything derived from the adjusted date (membership year, daily limit) inherits it.\n\nThe new acceptance test `Cp47Tests` (holiday-business-day) and the existing `Cp20Tests` (weekend rule) both pass, along with the rest of the suite.",
